e plus repository entry and disposable fixture arguments, shell=False. Baseline records only these five native occurrences and exact reviewed source hashes. Package source import/receipt bytes and validator path checks reviewed against retained preimages; no severity/rule exclusion or changed acceptance expectation. New observations pending; historical scanner hashes are not renewed. 2026-11-15 terminal progress: independent occurrence review approved exactly eight native Bandit candidates (B404 import and seven B603 calls) in the new controlled runner tests: absolute /bin/bash with fixed argv, shell=False, disposable fixture paths and internal data. Source and baseline hashes bind this disposition; all rules/severities remain enabled. Review and observed native reports: docs/validation/terminal-progress-20261115/review-security.json. This does not renew historical observations or approve the product. 2026-11-15 complete-run follow-up: independent review found eight benign native Bandit results across test_governance_diagnostics.py and test_historical_link_resolution.py: subprocess imports, fixed /bin/bash programs with positional disposable paths, fixed sys.executable governance/probe argv without shell=True, and /tmp/origin used only as rejected-path data. Exact post-Ruff native result objects from ox-security-bandit-yvDa5lcI were appended; the prior 109 entries remain unchanged. Native Bandit matching does not bind line/code; the pre-execution full-source and baseline SHA-256 guards enforce these reviewed inputs and reject drift. Both tests remain selected; all rules/severities remain enabled. Review and native inputs: docs/validation/bandit-repair-20261115/. New observations do not renew historical acceptance. 2026-11-16 OSV single acquisition clock: independent source review approved changes in test_database_age.py, test_backends.py and test_security_quality.py limited to helper/test names, timestamp cases and fake OSV report scenarios. No new subprocess or suppression; only these source hashes updated. Historical evidence is not renewed. See docs/validation/osv-acquisition-20261116/review.md."
